Virtual Pet Game
README
Authors: Jasmine Pruzan, Ishaan Bhalerao, Ellie Lo
Version: March 2026
Language: Java | GUI: Java Swing

================================================================

OVERVIEW

Virtual Pet Game is a desktop Java application where players
care for a digital pet of their choosing. You can adopt a dog,
cat, or fish, then keep it alive and happy by managing five
core stats: health, hunger, emotion, rest, and hygiene. Stats
are interconnected, so neglecting one will drag others down.
You earn money over time by performing care actions, which you
can spend at the in-game store on food and toys.

================================================================

GETTING STARTED

Prerequisites:
- Java 8 or higher
- Java Swing (included with the standard JDK)
- An IDE such as Eclipse, IntelliJ IDEA, or VS Code with Java

To run the application:
1. Clone or download the project repository.
2. Open it in your Java IDE.
3. Navigate to the VirtualPet package and run the main class.
4. Follow the on-screen prompts to name your pet and choose
   its type: Dog, Cat, or Fish.

================================================================

PROJECT STRUCTURE

pets
  Contains the Pet class, the core data model holding all pet
  state including stats, money, and toy inventory.

properties
  Contains all game logic classes: Food, Toys, Store, Health,
  Emotion, and Activities.

DrawingSurface
  Contains GUI handler classes including Button, which wires
  user interface actions to game logic.

VirtualPet
  Entry point package containing the main class that launches
  the application.

================================================================

CLASS REFERENCE

----------------------------------------------------------------
Pet  (pets.Pet)
----------------------------------------------------------------
The central data model of the game. Every piece of pet state
is stored and managed here.

The pet is initialized with a name and type. All five stats
(health, hunger, emotion, rest, hygiene) start at 10. The pet
starts with $100.00 and an empty toy inventory with a max of
5 slots.

All stat setters cap values at a maximum of 10. Calling
setHunger(), setRest(), or setHygiene() automatically triggers
the Health class to recalculate health. If all 5 toy slots are
full when setToys() is called, an error message is shown and
no toy is added.

----------------------------------------------------------------
Health  (properties.Health)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Manages how changes in hunger, rest, and hygiene affect the
pet's health stat. Called automatically when those stats change.

Hunger impact on health:
  - Hunger = 0         health -5
  - Hunger = 1 to 2    health -3
  - Hunger = 3 to 4    health -2
  - Hunger = 5 to 10   health +2

Rest impact on health:
  - Rest = 0           health -5
  - Rest = 1 to 4      health -1
  - Rest = 5 to 7      health +2
  - Rest = 8 to 10     health +3

Hygiene impact on health:
  - Hygiene = 0        health -5
  - Hygiene = 1 to 4   health -1
  - Hygiene = 5 to 10  health +2

If health is at or below 2, stat changes no longer reduce it
further. Only a vet visit can restore health at that point.
remindVetVisit() shows an urgent dialog when health hits 2
or below.

----------------------------------------------------------------
Emotion  (properties.Emotion)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Calculates the pet's happiness based on all other stats.

If any stat among health, hunger, rest, or hygiene is 3 or
below, emotion is forced down to 3.

If all four of those stats are 7 or above, emotion gains +7.

Otherwise emotion remains unchanged.

----------------------------------------------------------------
Food  (properties.Food)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Represents a purchasable food item with a name, target animal
type, price, and version (quality tier 1 through 4).

If food type matches the pet type, hunger increases by:
  Version 1 -> +2
  Version 2 -> +4
  Version 3 -> +6
  Version 4 -> +8

If food type does NOT match, the pet gains half the hunger
benefit and health is reduced by the same amount.

Dog food:
  Kibble Crunch ($10), Beef and Veggie Mix ($20),
  Chicken Feast ($30), Salmon Delight ($50),
  Lamb and Rice Bowl ($70), Golden Chicken Nuggets ($100)

Fish food:
  Flakes ($10), Algae Crisps ($20), Shrimp Pellets ($30),
  Spirulina Flakes ($50), Caviar Pearls ($70),
  Deep Abyss Infusion ($100)

Cat food:
  Five Fish Kibble ($10), Veggie Medley ($20),
  Expensive Melk ($30), Turkey and Cranberry Treats ($50),
  Bluefin Tuna Steak ($70), A Golden Rat ($100)

----------------------------------------------------------------
Toys  (properties.Toys)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Represents a purchasable toy with a name, target animal type,
price, and version (quality tier 1 through 4). Toys are stored
in the pet's inventory and chosen during play activities.

Dog toys:
  Used Ball ($4), Rubber Chew Bone ($8),
  Enchanted Chew Wand ($25), Guardian Plus Bear ($50),
  Dog God Worship Altar ($70), Goldenest Bone ($90)

Fish toys:
  Drift Ball ($4), Shell Hideout ($8),
  Biolume Bubble Machine ($25), Robotic Friend ($50),
  Ancient Calming Bell ($70), Platinum Speaker ($90)

Cat toys:
  Plain Kitty Sock ($4), Jingle Mouse ($8),
  Corner Scratch Post ($25), Laser Pointer ($50),
  Quarter Zip ($70), Legendary Airpods ($90)

----------------------------------------------------------------
Store  (properties.Store)
----------------------------------------------------------------
The in-game shop. Holds all food and toy inventories for each
animal type and handles all purchase transactions.

buyFood()    Deducts the food price from pet money, records
             the expense, and feeds the pet immediately.

buyToys()    Deducts the toy price, records the expense, and
             adds the toy to the pet's inventory.

vetVisit()   Costs $20 and resets pet health to 10. If the
             pet has less than $20, an error is shown and
             the visit is cancelled.

----------------------------------------------------------------
Button  (DrawingSurface.Button)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Handles user interaction from the GUI. Each instance is tied
to a specific action string and the active Pet object. Calling
actionPerformed() executes the corresponding game logic.

"Sleep"   Prompts the player to choose 1, 2, or 5 hours,
          calls the sleep activity, and awards the pet $10.

"Clean"   Runs the clean activity and awards the pet $10.

"Vet"     Calls the store's vet visit and awards $10 on
          success.

"Play"    Lists owned toys, prompts the player to pick one,
          runs the play activity with that toy, and awards
          the pet $10.

================================================================

STAT SYSTEM SUMMARY

All stats range from 0 to 10.

Health      Affected passively by hunger, rest, and hygiene.
            Only a vet visit restores it once it hits 2 or
            below.

Hunger      Decays over time. Restored by buying and feeding
            food from the store.

Emotion     Reflects the overall state of all other stats.
            Updates automatically when stats change.

Rest        Decays over time. Restored by sleeping.

Hygiene     Decays over time. Restored by the clean action.

================================================================

KNOWN ISSUES

- Health.addHygieneToHealth() has a variable declared as
  __newHealth__ instead of newHealth, causing a compile error.
  Rename the variable to fix it.

- Food.feedPet() uses currentHunger instead of currentHealth
  when calling p.setHealth() in the wrong-food-type branch.
  This is likely a logic bug and should be reviewed.

- The Toys version field is stored but not yet used in any
  play activity logic. Version-based play effects are not
  implemented.

- Store GUI navigation using CardLayout is partially commented
  out in Button.java and is pending re-implementation.

